cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Temporal Gamma Index for Time Series Forecast Evaluation"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. In academic work, please also cite the companion manuscript (see preferred-citation) once published."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Voyant
    given-names: Cyril
    website: "https://person.cyrilvoyant.com"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0242-7377"
repository-code: "https://github.com/cyrilvoyant/temporal-gamma-index"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-01-28
license: MIT
abstract: >
  MATLAB implementation of a tolerance-based, 3D Gamma Index framework for
  validating gridded spatio-temporal forecasts (solar irradiance, and more
  generally any gridded variable), adapting a method from radiotherapy dose
  verification (Low et al., 1998) to the double-penalty problem: classical
  pixel-wise scores such as RMSE/MAE over-penalize forecasts that are
  structurally correct but slightly displaced in space or time.
keywords:
  - gamma index
  - spatial verification
  - forecast verification
  - double penalty
  - gamma pass rate
  - time series forecasting
  - solar energy
  - solar irradiance
  - renewable energy
  - forecast metrics
preferred-citation:
  type: unpublished
  title: "A Tolerance-Based Framework for Spatio-Temporal Forecast Validation Using the Gamma-Index"
  authors:
    - name: "[anonymized for peer review]"
  year: 2026
  notes: "Preprint submitted to an Elsevier journal; under peer review. Update this entry with the final author list, journal, and DOI once published."
